# portal.env.example — copy to portal.env and fill in.
# portal.env is NOT committed (see .gitignore) — it contains deployment
# secrets/values; everything optional can stay commented out.

## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Bounding box for public issue submissions
## (hooks/submitIssue.go: PORTAL_MIN_LAT, PORTAL_MAX_LAT, PORTAL_MIN_LNG,
##  PORTAL_MAX_LNG; out-of-bounds reports are rejected with 400).
## The values below are only a placeholder — set the box around your
## property!
PORTAL_MIN_LAT=51.0
PORTAL_MAX_LAT=51.5
PORTAL_MIN_LNG=7.0
PORTAL_MAX_LNG=7.5

## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
## SMTP — NOT consumed by this env file!
## PocketBase SMTP settings are maintained by a superuser in the admin UI
## (/_/ → Settings → Mail settings), because the app itself never reads
## SMTP credentials from the environment. Keep the values only in the
## admin UI (and your password manager); document host/sender here for
## the operating team, WITHOUT password:
##   SMTP host:     mail.example.com
##   SMTP sender:    portal@example.com
##   SPF/DKIM/DMARC must be set up for the sender domain (plan.md).

## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
## S3 offsite backups — also NOT consumed from here directly.
## PocketBase backup S3 settings are maintained by a superuser in /_/
## (Settings → Backups → S3 storage). Until then, the nightly backup
## cron (0 2 * * *, keep 5, set by migration 1795000103) only writes
## local zip files under pb_data/backups/. Document the target here for
## the operating team, WITHOUT credentials:
##   S3 endpoint:    s3.example.com
##   S3 bucket:     weg-portal-backups
##   retention:      according to privacy policy / provider settings

## --------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Superusers: deliberately NOT configured via environment.
## Do NOT put superuser passwords in this file. The two superusers are
## created interactively on first start, see docs/deploy.md
## ("Ersteinrichtung: Superuser anlegen").
